@@ -72,6 +72,9 @@ This tool is especially useful as a final operation when piping through other to
 
    csvcut -c 9,1 examples/realdata/FY09_EDU_Recipients_by_State.csv | csvlook
 
+When :code:`--max-rows` is a positive number, csvlook only parses that many data rows. This makes it suitable for
+previewing a file whose later records may be large. A value of :code:`0` retains the ellipsis-only preview.
+
 If a data row contains more cells than the header row, csvlook will error. To fix the header row, use :doc:`csvclean`.
 
 To ignore the extra cells, instead:
